A: You've done a great job at isolating the important bits of the test and having a consistent understanding of both the theory being proven and the code being tested. I only have one minor correction and one minor nit-pick for you to consider.

Firstly, I don't see anything related to the index of an element in the array before and after removal in your contract test methods. Even though your methods are theoretically designed to deal with the ArrayList, it's likely that those particular functions don't hold any contract-specific assertions under the hood. You may want to augment your design to incorporate such tests, to ensure that your array manipulation logic functions as expected.

Secondly, NUnit assertions are usually used in their 'Assert' syntax, not as comments inside a test case. This would make them harder to read and debug. It's advisable that you refactor these into NUnit Assert statements, e.g.

```csharp
Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount, "Unexpected Count");
```

Let me know if you need more help.

